  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Malawians usually carry a Chichewa or Tumbuka first name with a meaning, an English or Christian name, or both. Chewa names are often thanks or hopes: Chikondi (love), Madalitso (blessings), Chisomo (grace), Tiyamike (let us praise), and many are unisex. English names are often virtues: Blessings, Gift, Chance, Precious, Loveness. The family name comes from the father: Chewa clan names like Banda, Phiri, Mwale and Tembo from the centre, Tumbuka names like Mkandawire, Gondwe, Nyirenda and Msiska from the north, Ngoni names like Jere and Maseko. Yao families in the south and along the lake are mostly Muslim and carry Arabic-derived names in a Malawian spelling, often ending in a vowel: Saidi, Kassimu, Salimu, Zainabu.",
